l class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). No account service is selected and authentication ships disabled by default, so this row cannot be assessed. There is no staff directory, so authorship cannot survive reassignment.</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="a-10 audit trail actor, time, action and affected revision are recorded"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>A-10</div><div><strong>Audit trail</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Actor, time, action and affected revision are recorded.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Assistant actions are journalled with work packets and raw task events, and takeoff evidence approval records a named reviewer with a timestamp (`src/studio/assistant/workPacketStore.ts`; SC-12 journey approved evidence for a named person). Remaining: there is no application-wide audit trail of actor, time, action and affected revision, and with no accounts the actor is not an authenticated identity.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="a-11 account recovery and offboarding removed staff cannot retain active organization access"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>A-11</div><div><strong>Account recovery and offboarding</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Removed staff cannot retain active organization access.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). No account service is selected and authentication ships disabled by default, so this row cannot be assessed. There is no offboarding path.</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="a-12 regional settings units, currency, date and timezone are explicit per project"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>A-12</div><div><strong>Regional settings</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Units, currency, date and timezone are explicit per project.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Units are fixed to millimetres by schema and currency is ISO-4217 validated per price book with an effective date and tax basis (`src/studio/architect/model.ts`, `priceBooks.ts`). Remaining: regional settings are not explicit or editable per project, and date and timezone handling is not declared.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="a-13 custom fields and classifications required fields validate and survive export/import"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>A-13</div><div><strong>Custom fields and classifications</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Required fields validate and survive export/import.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There are no user-defined custom fields or classifications, so validation and survival through export and import cannot be assessed.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="a-14 organization templates template revisions do not silently alter existing projects"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>A-14</div><div><strong>Organization templates</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Template revisions do not silently alter existing projects.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There are no organisation templates, so no template revision can alter an existing project. This is blocked behind the same missing account and organisation model as the rest of category A.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-B" data-category="B"><div class="cathead"><h2>B — Backups, saving and project lifecycle</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://construction.autodesk.com/workflows/construction-document-management/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Autodesk Forma construction document management</a> · <a href="https://www.oracle.com/construction-engineering/aconex/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Oracle Aconex</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="b-01 create and name projects unique ids survive duplicate display names"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Checked">✓</span>B-01</div><div><strong>Create and name projects</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Unique IDs survive duplicate display names.</p><small class="muted">State: verified (reviewed by Codex 2026-09-11, built browser on DANS1). The Project library creates and reopens two identically named projects with distinct IDs. Code: src/studio/ProjectLibrary.tsx, src/studio/projectRegistry.ts. Exact patch, 34 tests, dev/production journeys, fixture/build hashes and inspected desktop/tablet screenshots: proof/growth/2026-09-11-project-library/README.md. No installed/native platform claim.</small></div><span class="state">verified</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="b-02 automatic save feedback saved appears only after durable storage succeeds"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>B-02</div><div><strong>Automatic save feedback</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Saved appears only after durable storage succeeds.</p><small class="muted">State: partial. Re-verified in development 2026-09-08 for the main project record: &quot;saved · revision N&quot; appears only after a readback-verified write; an injected quota failure shows &quot;not confirmed saved&quot; with a retry that succeeds once storage recovers. Code/proof: [SC-02 protected saves](proof/growth/2026-09-08-az3-protected-saves/README.md), [walkthrough](walkthrough.md). Remaining: per-module records, production/native build.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="b-03 save as and duplicate copy gets new identity without sharing mutable records"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>B-03</div><div><strong>Save As and duplicate</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Copy gets new identity without sharing mutable records.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no Save As or duplicate action. The registry can shelve and switch projects but does not fork one into a new identity with independent mutable records.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="b-04 reopen recent projects latest saved revision and source sheets return after restart"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>B-04</div><div><strong>Reopen recent projects</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Latest saved revision and source sheets return after restart.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (updated 2026-09-11). Project library lists saved projects and reopens the exact project ID, revision 2 and original drawing after page reload, archive and restore. Code: src/studio/ProjectLibrary.tsx. Proof: proof/growth/2026-09-11-project-library/README.md. Remaining: full browser-process/installed-app restart with the same source fixture; a page reload is not that test.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="b-05 offline local storage airplane-mode restart restores drawings and attached originals"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>B-05</div><div><strong>Offline local storage</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Airplane-mode restart restores drawings and attached originals.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Storage is local first: drawings, price books and attached originals persist in browser storage and IndexedDB with no network dependency, and 