 with links and history intact"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>B-08</div><div><strong>Recycle bin</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Accidental removal is recoverable with links and history intact.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no recycle bin. Source-page archive and recover is the nearest behaviour and is assessed under D-04 and D-05.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="b-09 portable complete backup restore on a clean profile includes sources, models, rates and evidence"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>B-09</div><div><strong>Portable complete backup</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Restore on a clean profile includes sources, models, rates and evidence.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). Backup capture is real, with a versioned format, a 200 MB cap, an exclusion list and asset encoding, and restore impact is reviewed before any write. Applying a snapshot back into the workspace is deliberately not implemented and says so in the interface (`src/studio/BackupRestoreReview.tsx`: applying this snapshot is not available yet). Blocked on that slice; the takeoff-inventory replace path is a separate, narrower feature and does not satisfy this row.</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="b-10 backup integrity preview corrupt or missing assets block replacement before any write"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>B-10</div><div><strong>Backup integrity preview</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Corrupt or missing assets block replacement before any write.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Verified as a read-only integrity and impact milestone in the 2026-09-07 acceptance addendum in this file: packages and originals are 