ndent verifiers not refuted. Code/proof: [SC-02 protected saves](proof/growth/2026-09-08-az3-protected-saves/README.md). Remaining: per-module records (BOM, inventory, architecture, price books, sheet metadata), Web Lock lease, production/native build.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="b-13 storage failure recovery full disk/quota error preserves previous data and supports retry"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>B-13</div><div><strong>Storage failure recovery</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Full disk/quota error preserves previous data and supports retry.</p><small class="muted">State: partial. Main project record verified in development 2026-09-08: quota throw and silent-write failures keep the previously stored bytes byte-identical and the in-memory edit; an explicit retry persists it (store test plus tablet 1024x768 Fast CDP proof). Code/proof: [SC-02 protected saves](proof/growth/2026-09-08-az3-protected-saves/README.md). Remaining: IndexedDB originals/materials and per-module records, production/native build.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="b-14 migration and retention older supported backups upgrade with a reversible audit record"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>B-14</div><div><strong>Migration and retention</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Older supported backups upgrade with a reversible audit record.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). A supported legacy schema migrates forward and an unsupported one fails closed with the original bytes preserved, asserted by test (`src/studio/persistence.ts`). Remaining: migration is not reversible and produces no audit record, which is the substance of this row.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-C" data-category="C"><div class="cathead"><h2>C — CAD precision and drawing tools</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://www.autodesk.com/products/autocad" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Autodesk AutoCAD</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="c-01 lines, polylines, arcs and circles exact coordinates survive save and cad exchange"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-01</div><div><strong>Lines, polylines, arcs and circles</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Exact coordinates survive save and CAD exchange.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Lines, arcs and circles are authored entities and survive a hash-bound DXF round trip that restores stable IDs exactly (`src/studio/architect/model.ts`, `exchange.ts`; `architect.test.ts` &quot;DXF parametric round trip preserves stable IDs&quot;). A general open polyline entity does not exist: an imported LWPOLYLINE is exploded into separate lines. Remaining: a polyline entity, and coordinate survival through DWG and IFC rather than DXF alone.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-02 splines and curves control points and curve tolerance survive supported exchanges"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-02</div><div><strong>Splines and curves</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Control points and curve tolerance survive supported exchanges.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No spline or NURBS entity exists in the model schema. Curved geometry is limited to circles and arcs. There is nothing to assess until a curve type is authored.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-03 object snaps and tracking endpoint, midpoint, perpendicular and intersection picks are correct"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-03</div><div><strong>Object snaps and tracking</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Endpoint, midpoint, perpendicular and intersection picks are correct.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Seven snap kinds are computed geometrically and each is asserted independently, including line-circle and circle-circle intersections and a tangent at an irrational point (`src/studio/architect/precision.ts` snapPoint; `architect.test.ts` &quot;snap candidates resolve endpoint, midpoint, intersection, perpendicular, extension, centre and tangent&quot;; 72 tests logged 2026-09-10). Remaining: no inspected screenshot of live cursor snapping at the declared viewports, so the row stays partial under the tick rule.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-04 numeric and relative entry typed distance/angle yields the expected measured geometry"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-04</div><div><strong>Numeric and relative entry</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Typed distance/angle yields the expected measured geometry.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Typed length with ortho and polar angle stepping resolves to the exact constrained distance (`src/studio/architect/precision.ts` constrainPoint, asserted at 4500 mm on a 30 degree polar step). Remaining: typed angle and absolute or relative coordinate entry are not implemented, and there is no visual proof.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-05 coordinate systems and origins local and project origins transform without drift"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-05</div><div><strong>Coordinate systems and origins</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Local and project origins transform without drift.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). A single global millimetre space with level elevations is implemented. There is no user coordinate system, origin relocation or rotated working plane, so the row cannot be assessed.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-06 layers and visibility hidden, locked and isolated layers retain correct entity membership"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-06</div><div><strong>Layers and visibility</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Hidden, locked and isolated layers retain correct entity membership.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No CAD drafting layer exists. The model field named layers is a wall assembly material layer, not a visibility or lock container, and DXF export synthesises layer names from levels. Recorded explicitly because the field name invites a false positive.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-07 selection and properties window/crossing selection and batch edits affect intended objects only"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-07</div><div><strong>Selection and properties</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Window/crossing selection and batch edits affect intended objects only.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Selection is a single entity id. Window and crossing selection, multi-select and batch property edits are not implemented.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-08 move, rotate, scale and copy transform and undo preserve dimensions and ids"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-08</div><div><strong>Move, rotate, scale and copy</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Transform and undo preserve dimensions and IDs.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Move, rotate, scale, copy and array are not implemented as transforms. Offset and mirror each derive one copy, which does not satisfy this row.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-09 offset, trim, extend and fillet edge cases retain valid connected geometry"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-09</div><div><strong>Offset, trim, extend and fillet</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Edge cases retain valid connected geometry.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Offset, mirror, trim, extend and a tangential fillet are real solvers with asserted results and explicit edge-case refusals: a radius too large for its segments, parallel segments that cannot meet, and an intersection already inside the segment are each rejected with a stated reason (`src/studio/architect/precision.ts`; `architect.test.ts` &quot;precision exact length, mirror, offset, trim, extend and tangential fillet&quot;). Remaining: no inspected screenshot, and connected-geometry survival is proven per operation rather than across a drawing session.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-10 blocks and reusable symbols definition update changes intended instances without broken attributes"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-10</div><div><strong>Blocks and reusable symbols</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Definition update changes intended instances without broken attributes.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No block, symbol or instance definition exists.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-11 constraints and parameters driving dimension regenerates dependent geometry consistently"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-11</div><div><strong>Constraints and parameters</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Driving dimension regenerates dependent geometry consistently.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No geometric or dimensional constraint solver exists. Wall-hosted dimensions report geometry; they do not drive it.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-12 dimensions, leaders and text annotation values update and plot legibly at scale"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-12</div><div><strong>Dimensions, leaders and text</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Annotation values update and plot legibly at scale.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Wall-hosted dimensions are associative: moving a wall end from 4000 to 5000 mm regenerates the annotation text, and plan, elevation and section views regenerate with it (`src/studio/architect/drawing.ts`; `architect.test.ts` &quot;plan, elevations, sections and associative dimensions regenerate after editing&quot;). Remaining: free-standing linear, aligned, angular and radial dimensions, leaders and user-placed text do not exist, and plotted legibility at scale is unproven.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-13 hatches, lineweights and plot styles screen and exported output agree on declared styles"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-13</div><div><strong>Hatches, lineweights and plot styles</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Screen and exported output agree on declared styles.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Hatching is genuine scanline geometry with ring containment and hole exclusion across five patterns, and per-primitive widths are emitted for plan, elevation and section output (`src/studio/architect/drawing.ts` hatchLines). Remaining: no user control of lineweight, colour or plot style, and no proof that screen and exported PDF agree on declared styles.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-14 undo, redo and transaction history one user operation undoes atomically without losing active context"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-14</div><div><strong>Undo, redo and transaction history</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: One user operation undoes atomically without losing active context.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Undo and redo form a two-stack history capped at 60 steps with redo invalidated on a new edit, bound to Ctrl+Z and Ctrl+Y, and one architect operation is one transaction (`src/studio/architect/ArchitectWorkspace.tsx`). The assistant undo path is separately proven in the SC-08 journeys. Remaining: history is cleared on project load, so undo does not survive a reopen, and no inspected screenshot covers the keyboard path.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-D" data-category="D"><div class="cathead"><h2>D — Documents, sheets and drawing registers</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://www.autodesk.com/products/autocad" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Autodesk AutoCAD</a> · <a href="https://www.bluebeam.com/product/markups-and-data/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bluebeam markups and data</a> · <a href="https://www.oracle.com/construction-engineering/aconex/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Oracle Aconex</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="d-01 multi-file and multi-page import pdfs with different page sizes preserve every original page"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-01</div><div><strong>Multi-file and multi-page import</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: PDFs with different page sizes preserve every original page.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Multi-page PDF import stores each page with its own identity and dimensions, and a 13-page Redburn set was imported and retained through native runs (SC-10, SC-13). Remaining: a fixture with deliberately mixed page sizes has not been asserted page by page.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-02 sheet names and numbers rename changes labels without breaking evidence references"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-02</div><div><strong>Sheet names and numbers</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Rename changes labels without breaking evidence references.</p><small class="muted">State: partial — verified in development 2026-09-08 for source sheets: rename changes only the page label/discipline; calibrations, traces, items, annotations and saved views stay keyed by original page index and byte-identical; the new name shows in the register, heading and navigation after reload. Fixture Redburn BR250157 (SHA-256 b57956f76b5dc893ac2b28a021f3f92e345807e326d6b1f8313e373f9145ad38, 13 pages); 37 focused tests; three verifiers not refuted. Code/proof: [SC-03 sheets](proof/growth/2026-09-08-az3-sheets/README.md). Remaining: authored architectural sheets, production/native build.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-03 add and duplicate drawing sheets new sheet receives an independent identity and layout"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-03</div><div><strong>Add and duplicate drawing sheets</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: New sheet receives an independent identity and layout.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Authored sheets can be added, duplicated, renamed, reordered, archived and recovered, each with an independent identity and layout, and duplication does not share viewport records (`src/studio/architect/authoredSheetSet.ts`, tests pass 2026-09-10). Remaining: no inspected screenshot of the authored sheet lifecycle at the declared viewports.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-04 remove with impact preview review lists dependent takeoffs, links and viewports before removal"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-04</div><div><strong>Remove with impact preview</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Review lists dependent takeoffs, links and viewports before removal.</p><small class="muted">State: partial — verified in development 2026-09-08 for source-page archive (the product&#39;s removal): the review lists calibrations, measured traces, located items, annotations, linked photos and, newly, saved views for that page, and storage stays unchanged until confirmation. Code/proof: [SC-03 sheets](proof/growth/2026-09-08-az3-sheets/README.md). Remaining: whole-source removal, SHA-bound construction takeoff registers (not page-scoped, so not counted), production/native build.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-05 restore removed sheets restored sheet recovers annotations, scale and original ordering"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-05</div><div><strong>Restore removed sheets</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Restored sheet recovers annotations, scale and original ordering.</p><small class="muted">State: partial — verified in development 2026-09-08 as archive → recover: the page returns to its original managed slot with identical metadata, its locked scale and a real sketch annotation byte-identical after recover and reload (unit test with job evidence after archive and recover; browser assertions on 13 calibrations and the annotation at every step). Code/proof: [SC-03 sheets](proof/growth/2026-09-08-az3-sheets/README.md). Remaining: authored sheets, production/native build.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-06 reorder and group sheets discipline groups and order persist after restart and export"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-06</div><div><strong>Reorder and group sheets</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Discipline groups and order persist after restart and export.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Verified in the 2026-09-07 acceptance addendum in this file for source-sheet discipline groups, persistent managed order and an actual ordered-register download, retaining every original page identity through reload in browser and Windows-native runs. Remaining: the export is a JSON register, and authored multi-sheet publishing and reordering the source PDF itself are outside that acceptance.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-07 title blocks and templates project metadata updates linked fields without clipping"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-07</div><div><strong>Title blocks and templates</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Project metadata updates linked fields without clipping.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no title block or template system, so project metadata cannot update linked fields.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-08 viewports and per-view scale independent scales measure correctly in exported pdf"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-08</div><div><strong>Viewports and per-view scale</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Independent scales measure correctly in exported PDF.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). A sheet carries up to twelve viewports with independent view, level, scale and position, and resizing the paper refits frames without altering viewport scales (`src/studio/architect/authoredSheetSet.ts`). Export is real vector PDF (`sheets.ts`). Remaining: measuring an exported PDF at each declared viewport scale has not been executed.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-09 drawing revisions and supersession old revision remains retrievable and visibly superseded"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-09</div><div><strong>Drawing revisions and supersession</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Old revision remains retrievable and visibly superseded.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Drawing revisions and supersession do not exist. The project carries a revision counter, but old drawing revisions are not retrievable or visibly superseded.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-10 revision overlay and slip-sheeting added/deleted geometry is inspectable with alignment controls"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-10</div><div><strong>Revision overlay and slip-sheeting</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Added/deleted geometry is inspectable with alignment controls.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no revision overlay or slip-sheeting, so added and deleted geometry cannot be inspected between issues.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-11 ocr and sheet indexing suggested names are reviewable and uncertainty is visible"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-11</div><div><strong>OCR and sheet indexing</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Suggested names are reviewable and uncertainty is visible.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no OCR or automatic sheet indexing, and therefore no suggested names or visible uncertainty.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-12 cross-sheet references and hyperlinks detail callout opens the intended sheet revision"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-12</div><div><strong>Cross-sheet references and hyperlinks</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Detail callout opens the intended sheet revision.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Cross-sheet references and detail callouts are not implemented.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-13 batch printing and issue sets selected sheets export in reviewed order with an issue register"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-13</div><div><strong>Batch printing and issue sets</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Selected sheets export in reviewed order with an issue register.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no batch printing or issue set. Single-sheet PDF export exists and is assessed under D-08.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-14 bookmarks and saved views personal navigation restores the correct page and viewport"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-14</div><div><strong>Bookmarks and saved views</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Personal navigation restores the correct page and viewport.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Verified in the 2026-09-07 acceptance addendum in this file for local original-page, zoom and source-relative-centre bookmarks, with pan, zoom, page switching, viewport restoration, resize, reload, removal and failed-write preservation passing, and a tablet sub-check at both declared orientations. Remaining: saved views are local project metadata, with no account synchronisation or sharing.</small><