 transform, and is stored per page with duplicate page records rejected and version-1 records migrated (`src/studio/calibration.ts`; `calibration.test.ts`). Remaining: measurement after a deliberate sheet rotation and reload is asserted at transform level, not through an inspected UI journey.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-02 separate axes and distorted scans calibration records anisotropy or blocks unsupported measurement"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-02</div><div><strong>Separate axes and distorted scans</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Calibration records anisotropy or blocks unsupported measurement.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Calibration refuses zero-length points, singular transforms and inconsistent converted distances, and records declared, inferred and manual provenance with conflict detection that is independent of candidate order and requires explicit resolution (`src/studio/calibration.ts` reconcileCalibrationCandidates). Remaining: anisotropic separately scaled axes are not represented, so distorted scans are refused rather than measured.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-03 lengths, perimeters and counts totals match independently measured fixture values"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-03</div><div><strong>Lengths, perimeters and counts</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Totals match independently measured fixture values.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Length, area, count and sketch measurements exist with tracing runs, gates and topology validation (`src/studio/tracing.ts`, `src/studio/store.ts`; tracing suites pass 2026-09-10). The SC-12 journey traced a run at 5.000 m against a locked 5 m calibration. Remaining: totals are not reconciled against an independently measured fixture across a whole sheet set.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-04 areas, holes and net deductions openings subtract once and self-intersections are rejected"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-04</div><div><strong>Areas, holes and net deductions</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Openings subtract once and self-intersections are rejected.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Area measurement subtracts openings through real polygon boolean geometry, and the architect model proves an opening removes exact material volume once, a T intersection is a union rather than a sum, and overlapping or duplicate hosted openings are rejected (`src/studio/architect/geometry.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: net deduction is proven in the design model, not for user-drawn takeoff polygons with holes on a source sheet.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-05 volumes, slopes and elevations 3d quantity basis distinguishes projected from actual surface"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-05</div><div><strong>Volumes, slopes and elevations</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: 3D quantity basis distinguishes projected from actual surface.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Volume carries an explicit basis: the area-depth method names its calibration and every depth evidence id, and results are re-verified against their operands and job revision so a stale snapshot is refused (`src/studio/construction/quantity.ts`). Remaining: projected versus actual sloped surface area is not distinguished, which is the substance of this row.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-06 trade and work-package classification reclassification updates totals without duplicate measurements"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-06</div><div><strong>Trade and work-package classification</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Reclassification updates totals without duplicate measurements.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Quantities group by trade only. There is no work-package or standard classification such as NRM, Uniclass or CSI, and therefore no reclassification behaviour to assess.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-07 assembly breakdowns element quantity decomposes into explicit materials and assumptions"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-07</div><div><strong>Assembly breakdowns</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Element quantity decomposes into explicit materials and assumptions.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Element quantities decompose into material rows with declared density, rate revision and waste, and design material sync is idempotent, preserves physical rows, invalidates a changed review and retires deletions (`src/studio/architect/materialBridge.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: assumptions are recorded per material rather than presented as a reviewable assembly breakdown.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-08 duplicate detection and exclusions overlapping takeoffs are reviewable before totaling"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-08</div><div><strong>Duplicate detection and exclusions</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Overlapping takeoffs are reviewable before totaling.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Overlapping takeoffs are not detected or presented for review before totalling.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-09 revision quantity comparison additions, removals and changed quantities reconcile prior issue"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-09</div><div><strong>Revision quantity comparison</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Additions, removals and changed quantities reconcile prior issue.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no revision comparison that reconciles additions, removals and changed quantities against a prior issue.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-10 measurement source links each quantity opens exact page, region and source revision"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-10</div><div><strong>Measurement source links</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Each quantity opens exact page, region and source revision.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Every calculation operand requires at least one evidence reference, and document, calibration and photo evidence identity and digests are cross-validated (`src/studio/bomContract.ts`; BOM suites pass 2026-09-10). Remaining: opening the exact page region from a quantity is not proven by an inspected journey.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-11 stock lengths, packs and wastage purchased quantities remain distinct from net measured demand"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-11</div><div><strong>Stock lengths, packs and wastage</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Purchased quantities remain distinct from net measured demand.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Waste is applied as a percentage that produces an order quantity distinct from net measured demand on architect wall layers (`src/studio/architect/geometry.ts`; `architect.test.ts` quantity and cost use net geometry, explicit density, rate revision and waste). Remaining: stock lengths and pack sizes are not modelled, and waste is unavailable on source-sheet takeoff markups.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-12 manual, model and ai quantity provenance user can distinguish and review each quantity origin"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-12</div><div><strong>Manual, model and AI quantity provenance</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: User can distinguish and review each quantity origin.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Provenance is enforced rather than optional: calibration candidates carry method, evidence and document id, and a candidate with empty evidence is rejected by test. Assistant-created measurements carry tool receipts bound to a revision (SC-12). Remaining: manual, model and AI origins are not surfaced as a single reviewable distinction in the interface.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-13 reconciliation and audit exports summary totals reproduce detailed rows with units and rounding"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-13</div><div><strong>Reconciliation and audit exports</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Summary totals reproduce detailed rows with units and rounding.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Money totals are summed in integer minor units grouped by currency, tax basis and decimal places, so summary figures reproduce their rows without floating-point drift, and CSV export escapes formula-leading cells (`src/studio/priceBooks.ts`). Remaining: a reconciliation export that reproduces detailed rows with units and declared rounding is not implemented.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-14 bulk edit, undo and recovery batch operation restores all affected 