n></article><article class="requirement" data-search="u-07 multi-monitor and high-dpi desktop dialogs and text remain visible at tested scaling levels"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-07</div><div><strong>Multi-monitor and high-DPI desktop</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Dialogs and text remain visible at tested scaling levels.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Multi-monitor and high-DPI scaling have not been tested and no scaling levels are declared.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="u-08 progress, cancellation and background jobs long operation shows honest status and can be stopped"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-08</div><div><strong>Progress, cancellation and background jobs</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Long operation shows honest status and can be stopped.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Long assistant operations show honest status and can be stopped, with a stop preserving completed tool receipts and denying a pending permission prompt, and provider requests abort and discard late responses (`src/studio/assistant/useAssistantChat.ts`, `src/lib/pricingResearch.server.ts`). Remaining: import, export and build operations do not report progress or support cancellation uniformly.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="u-09 useful validation and empty states user can recover from invalid input without losing edits"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-09</div><div><strong>Useful validation and empty states</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: User can recover from invalid input without losing edits.</p><small class="muted">State: partial. Navigation milestone verified 2026-09-08; full row remains open. Code/proof: [Stage07 scoped results, source diff and executed evidence](proof/growth/2026-09-08-07-walkthrough-release/index.html). Latest bounded milestone: [Stage09 clean plans, boundaries, body reach and release evidence](proof/growth/2026-09-08-09-walkthrough-polish/index.html); full row stays open.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="u-10 bulk operations and multi-selection preview clearly reports affected items before applying changes"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-10</div><div><strong>Bulk operations and multi-selection</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Preview clearly reports affected items before applying changes.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no multi-selection or bulk operation, so no affected-items preview exists. Related absence is recorded at C-07 and T-14.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="u-11 per-user preferences and units preference changes do not reinterpret existing geometry"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-11</div><div><strong>Per-user preferences and units</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Preference changes do not reinterpret existing geometry.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Preferences are validated and migrated rather than trusted, and legacy appearance settings migrate while malformed values are refused without corrupting stored settings (appearance and menu preference suites pass 2026-09-10). Units are fixed to millimetres, so a preference change cannot reinterpret geometry. Remaining: there is no per-user unit choice to test against.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="u-12 localization and terminology industry-specific terms do not change underlying data meaning"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-12</div><div><strong>Localization and terminology</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Industry-specific terms do not change underlying data meaning.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no localisation or terminology mapping.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="u-13 onboarding and sample isolation sample work cannot be mistaken for the user&#39;s source project"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-13</div><div><strong>Onboarding and sample isolation</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Sample work cannot be mistaken for the user&#39;s source project.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Sample and demonstration data are firewalled from verified output: sample sources are flagged, the assistant reports origin and sample status when reading a building, and fixture data is barred from verified price and quote outputs (`src/studio/assistant/workbenchStructure.ts`, `read_source_building` origin and sample fields). Remaining: there is no onboarding flow, and the separation is proven in tool contracts rather than an inspected journey.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="u-14 support diagnostics and recovery guidance export omits secrets and includes reproducible failure context"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-14</div><div><strong>Support diagnostics and recovery guidance</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Export omits secrets and includes reproducible failure context.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no support diagnostic export, so secret omission and reproducible failure context cannot be assessed.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-V" data-category="V"><div class="cathead"><h2>V — Versioning, collaboration and staff handoff</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://helpcenter.graphisoft.com/user-guide/134439/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Graphisoft BIMcloud teams</a> · <a href="https://www.buildingsmart.org/standards/bsi-standards/bim-collaboration-format/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">buildingSMART BCF</a> · <a href="https://www.oracle.com/construction-engineering/aconex/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Oracle Aconex</a> · <a href="https://construction.autodesk.com/workflows/construction-document-management/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Autodesk Forma construction document management</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="v-01 named project versions saved milestone reopens exact drawing, sources and commercial state"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>V-01</div><div><strong>Named project versions</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Saved milestone reopens exact drawing, sources and commercial state.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Project and design revisions increment only on a real structural change, a no-op keeps the revision, and stale writes are refused against the last loaded bytes (`src/studio/architect/model.ts` revise; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: there is no browsable version history to restore from.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="v-02 change comparisons reviewer can inspect changed objects, quantities, documents and rates"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>V-02</div><div><strong>Change comparisons</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Reviewer can inspect changed objects, quantities, documents and rates.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no change comparison across objects, quantities, documents and rates.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="v-03 staff handoff package fresh recipient profile restores complete reviewed project context"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>V-03</div><div><strong>Staff handoff package</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Fresh recipient profile restores complete reviewed project context.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). A portable backup captures sources, design and rates in a versioned format with an asset manifest, and restore impact is reviewable (`src/studio/projectBackup.ts`). Remaining: a fresh recipient profile cannot restore it because applying a snapshot is not implemented (B-09), so the handoff is not complete.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="v-04 selective package content private rates and unrelated documents are excluded by review"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>V-04</div><div><strong>Selective package content</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Private rates and unrelated documents are excluded by review.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Package content cannot be selected or reviewed for exclusion, so private rates cannot be withheld.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="v-05 recipient and distribution list intended staff and access level are visible before sending"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>V-05</div><div><strong>Recipient and distribution list</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Intended staff and access level are visible before sending.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). The external handoff bridge returns an explicit unavailable result by design and no recipient or access level can be chosen (`src/studio/crmBridge.ts`). Blocked on an account service and an authenticated transport.</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="v-06 transmittals and receipts sent status requires durable receipt rather than button click"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>V-06</div><div><strong>Transmittals and receipts</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Sent status requires durable receipt rather than button click.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). Nothing is sent, so no durable receipt exists. The bridge reports unavailable rather than implying delivery, which is the honest state but not a pass.</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="v-07 download links and expiry revoked or expired link cannot fetch protected documents"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>V-07</div><div><strong>Download links and expiry</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Revoked or expired link cannot fetch protected documents.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). There are no download links, expiry or revocation.</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="v-08 assignments and notifications task owner receives only relevant authorized information"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>V-08</div><div><strong>Assignments and notifications</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Task owner receives only relevant authorized information.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Assignments and notifications are not implemented.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="v-09 comments and review decisions replies retain authorship and referenced revision"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>V-09</div><div