cation.md; LATEST-VERIFIED-BUILD.md). Remaining: builds run from an uncommitted working tree, so a commit and dirty-diff record is not part of the identity.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-02 desktop install and upgrade upgrade retains real user profile and compatible project data"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-02</div><div><strong>Desktop install and upgrade</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Upgrade retains real user profile and compatible project data.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No build has been installed over the normal application. Every verified package runs from an isolated profile and the register must not imply an upgrade path was tested.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-03 offline cold start installed app opens source and design without development services"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-03</div><div><strong>Offline cold start</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Installed app opens source and design without development services.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). The packaged Windows application starts and completes journeys from an isolated profile without development services, including retained sheets, price books and saved views (SC-11, SC-13 native runs). Remaining: cold start is proven for the packaged executable, not for an installed application.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-04 web production parity built site completes the same declared workflows as development"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-04</div><div><strong>Web production parity</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Built site completes the same declared workflows as development.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Each release runs the same declared journeys against the built site and the native application, most recently 40 runs and 765 commands across both for build 8e14ac427997. Remaining: parity is asserted for the declared journeys only, with rendering web-only and the native refusal documented.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-05 dependency and license inventory bundled components carry required notices and versions"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-05</div><div><strong>Dependency and license inventory</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Bundled components carry required notices and versions.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no dependency and licence inventory with required notices. A bundled third-party CAD engine and a CC0 asset are recorded individually in their slices, which does not satisfy this row.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-06 security and tenant isolation adversarial access tests cannot cross project permissions"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-06</div><div><strong>Security and tenant isolation</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Adversarial access tests cannot cross project permissions.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). There are no tenants or permissions to cross. Provider keys are confined to server modules (X-10), but adversarial access testing has no boundary to attack until accounts exist.</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-07 backup/restore disaster drill clean machine restoration proves complete recoverability"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-07</div><div><strong>Backup/restore disaster drill</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Clean machine restoration proves complete recoverability.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). Backup capture and restore preflight are real, but applying a snapshot is not implemented, so a clean-machine restoration drill cannot be completed. Blocked with B-09.</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-08 observability without secrets error reports omit keys, private prompts and unauthorized documents"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-08</div><div><strong>Observability without secrets</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Error reports omit keys, private prompts and unauthorized documents.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Keys are read only in server modules and never appear in responses, failures or browser code, and evidence bundles are reviewed before archiving (`src/lib/pricingResearch.server.ts`). Remaining: there is no error reporting pipeline to audit for private prompts or unauthorised documents.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-09 performance and resource limits oversized files fail safely without freezing or partial writes"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-09</div><div><strong>Performance and resource limits</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Oversized files fail safely without freezing or partial writes.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Oversized and malformed inputs fail safely rather than corrupting state: workbook import is bounded against zip expansion, backup capture is capped, the CAD bridge enforces a size limit with cancellation, and a failed write preserves the previously stored bytes. Remaining: no freeze or partial-write behaviour has been measured under a deliberate resource-exhaustion test.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-10 rollback and forward compatibility failed upgrade can recover last confirmed data revision"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-10</div><div><strong>Rollback and forward compatibility</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Failed upgrade can recover last confirmed data revision.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). A newer stored revision is never silently overwritten and an unsupported schema fails closed with the original bytes intact, so the last confirmed data revision survives a refused change (`src/studio/persistence.ts`, `store.ts`). Remaining: there is no application upgrade path, so upgrade rollback is untested.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-11 support and incident handling reproducible ticket links diagnostics, affected build and recovery"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-11</div><div><strong>Support and incident handling</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Reproducible ticket links diagnostics, affected build and recovery.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no incident or ticket handling linking diagnostics to an affected build.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-12 proof expiry after changes dependency changes reopen affected completed acceptance rows"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-12</div><div><strong>Proof expiry after changes</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Dependency changes reopen affected completed acceptance rows.</p><small class="muted">State: verified (assessed 2026-09-10). Stated as a governing rule of this register and applied in practice: a dependency change reopens its acceptance, superseded builds are marked superseded rather than deleted, and on 2026-09-10 every row was re-assessed against shipping code with stale claims corrected. Earlier candidate builds remain recorded as superseded with their failures preserved.</small></div><span class="state">verified</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-13 release notes and capability contract users see delivered limits and verified platform support"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-13</div><div><strong>Release notes and capability contract</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Users see delivered limits and verified platform support.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). The verified build record states what the build delivers, its digests, and its known limits including the eight-step assistant pause, web-only rendering and the untested two-window native case (LATEST-VERIFIED-BUILD.md). Remaining: this is a repository record rather than release notes visible to a user inside the application.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-14 full working-day acceptance named industry scenario completes create-to-handover-to-reopen with proof"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-14</div><div><strong>Full working-day acceptance</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Named industry scenario completes create-to-handover-to-reopen with proof.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No named industry scenario has completed the create-to-handover-to-reopen working day. Handover cannot complete while external delivery is unavailable (V-05) and backup apply is unimplemented (B-09). All 68 industry profiles remain not-tested.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article></section></div></section>
 <section><h2>One complete working day</h2><p>Each industry profile must complete all eight stages using its own representative fixture and outputs. Include restart, cancellation, permission boundaries, a source revision and clean-profile recovery.</p><details><summary>DAY-01 · Start/reopen</summary><p>Open the correct job after a full restart; confirm identity, latest revision, source availability, permissions and unsaved-change status.</p></details><details><summary>DAY-02 · Receive work</summary><p>Import a new source/revision, name and group its sheets, verify scale/origin, compare changes and retain the prior issue.</p></details><details><summary>DAY-03 · Design/measure</summary><p>Perform the profile-specific drawing, modeling or measurement; edit, undo and redo; verify associated schedules and quantities.</p></details><details><summary>DAY-04 · Check/review</summary><p>Run appropriate geometric/information/calculation checks; record source, assumptions, issues and an authorized review decision.</p></details><details><summary>DAY-05 · Price/procure</summary><p>Import a supplier workbook or request bounded pricing research; compare units and variants; approve selected rates; reconcile the estimate.</p></details><details><summary>DAY-06 · Issue/handoff</summary><p>Select exact drawings, evidence and commercial content; prepare package for named staff; verify recipient access/import and durable receipt where sending is implemented.</p></details><details><summary>DAY-07 · Use on site</summary><p>Open offline field package, record an inspection/change/photo and synchronize with conflict review when reconnected.</p></details><details><summary>DAY-08 · End/recover</summary><p>Save, export complete backup, archive and restore; on clean profile verify originals, design, quantities, prices and history.</p></details></section>
 <section><h2>68 industry and professional scenarios</h2><p>The industry filter above selects applicable requirement categories. Profiles share project, document, cost, access, exchange, collaboration and release foundations.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Profile</th><th>Daily scenario</th><th>Input</th><th>Required output</th><th>State</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr data-profile="IND-01"><td><strong>Residential architecture</strong><br>Architect / building designer</td><td>Develop an alteration with existing/new/demolished work</td><td>Survey and client brief</td><td>Coordinated plans, sections, schedules and issue set</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-02"><td><strong>Commercial architecture</strong><br>Architect / design manager</td><td>Coordinate a multi-tenant commercial fit-out</td><td>Base build, tenancy requirements and consultant models</td><td>Coordinated design, room data and consultant issues</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-03"><td><strong>High-rise and mixed-use</strong><br>Architect / BIM lead</td><td>Coordinate repeated floors, cores and facade variants</td><td>Tower models and level schedule</td><td>Level-aware quantities, coordinated core and issue packages</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-04"><td><strong>Drafting and documentation services</strong><br>Draftsperson / CAD technician</td><td>Turn approved markups into a revised drawing set</td><td>Redlines, CAD standards and prior issue</td><td>Dimensioned drawings, checked references and change register</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-05"><td><strong>BIM coordination and digital engineering</strong><br>BIM coordinator / information manager</td><td>Federate consultants and resolve clashes</td><td>IFC models, origins and information requirements</td><td>BCF issues, checked properties and coordinated federation</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-06"><td><strong>Interior design and fit-out</strong><br>Interior designer / fit-out contractor</td><td>Specify finishes, joinery and furniture for a tenancy</td><td>Room brief and measured existing shell</td><td>Finish schedules, reflected ceiling plans and procurement list</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-07"><td><strong>Heritage and conservation</strong><br>Conservation architect / heritage consultant</td><td>Document repairs while retaining existing fabric</td><td>Historic records, scans and condition survey</td><td>Fabric map, repair schedule and intervention record</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-08"><td><strong>Urban design and planning</strong><br>Urban designer / planner</td><td>Compare precinct massing and public-realm options</td><td>GIS constraints, terrain and planning brief</td><td>Option study, area schedule and consultation package</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-09"><td><strong>Landscape architecture</strong><br>Landscape architect</td><td>Design planting and hardscape around a building</td><td>Survey, planting brief and drainage plan</td><td>Planting schedule, grading and maintenance package</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-10"><td><strong>Arboriculture and ecology</strong><br>Arborist / ecologist</td><td>Review tree protection and habitat impacts</td><td>Tree survey, habitat mapping and site design</td><td>Protection zones, impact register and mitigation plan</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-11"><td><strong>Surveying and cadastral work</strong><br>Surveyor</td><td>Adjust survey observations and issue site control</td><td>GNSS/total-station observations and control</td><td>Checked coordinates, closure report and survey plan</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-12"><td><strong>Reality capture and scan-to-BIM</strong><br>Survey technician / modeler</td><td>Record a complex existing building and review derived geometry</td><td>Point clouds, photos and control targets</td><td>Registered cloud, residual report and source-linked model</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-13"><td><strong>Civil and land development</strong><br>Civil engineer</td><td>Design a serviced subdivision</td><td>Terrain, boundaries and utility records</td><td>Grading, roads, services, quantities and civil sheets</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-14"><td><strong>Earthworks and excavation</strong><br>Earthworks estimator / contractor</td><td>Price and stage a cut/fill operation</td><td>Existing/proposed surfaces and ground investigation</td><td>Volume reconciliation, haul assumptions and work packages</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-15"><td><strong>Roads and highways</strong><br>Road designer / transport engineer</td><td>Revise a corridor and intersection</td><td>Alignment criteria, survey and drainage</td><td>Plans, profiles, cross-sections and quantities</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-16"><td><strong>Rail and transit</strong><br>Rail engineer / station designer</td><td>Coordinate track, platform and station services</td><td>Rail alignment, envelope and station requirements</td><td>Chainage drawings, clearances and systems coordination</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-17"><td><strong>Airports and aviation infrastructure</strong><br>Airfield engineer / terminal designer</td><td>Coordinate apron or terminal works</td><td>Airside survey, operations constraints and services</td><td>Pavement/service layouts and phased issue package</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-18"><td><strong>Ports, coastal and marine infrastructure</strong><br>Marine/civil engineer</td><td>Plan a wharf retrofit with operating constraints</td><td>Bathymetry, structural survey and asset records</td><td>Coordinated marine works and inspected asset handover</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-19"><td><strong>Traffic and transport planning</strong><br>Transport planner</td><td>Check access and circulation around a site</td><td>Site plan, vehicle assumptions and movement demand</td><td>Swept paths, access option study and assumptions report</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-20"><td><strong>Stormwater, drainage and flood studies</strong><br>Hydrologist / drainage engineer</td><td>Test a drainage upgrade under defined rainfall scenarios</td><td>Catchments, rainfall data, pipes and levels</td><td>Hydraulic results, flood extents and design report</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-21"><td><strong>Water and wastewater utilities</strong><br>Water engineer / asset operator</td><td>Upgrade a pressure or wastewater network</td><td>Asset GIS, demand and operating data</td><td>Checked network scenario and construction/operations package</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-22"><td><strong>Geotechnical and ground engineering</strong><br>Geotechnical engineer</td><td>Assess excavation beside an existing structure</td><td>Boreholes, soil tests and groundwater</td><td>Staged analysis, displacement results and reviewed report</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-23"><td><strong>Structural steel buildings</strong><br>Structural engineer / steel detailer</td><td>Design and detail a braced industrial building</td><td>Architectural geometry and design actions</td><td>Checked model, connection package and fabrication drawings</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-24"><td><strong>Concrete and precast construction</strong><br>Structural engineer / precast detailer</td><td>Coordinate reinforcement, embeds and erection</td><td>Structural model, member design and supplier constraints</td><td>Bar schedules, cast units and installation package</td><td>Not tested</td></tr><tr data-profile="IND-25"><td><strong>Timber and mass-timber construction</strong><br>Timber engineer / fabricator</td><td>Coordinate panel joints and erection</td><td>Architectural model and material/connection data</td><td>Checked panels, cut lists and assembly instructions</td><td>Not