+"I-01","Interoperability, imports and integrations","DXF import/export","Independent reader verifies supported geometry, layers and units","partial","src/studio/architect/exchange.ts","","ACAD; DWG; BCF; IDS","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). DXF export and import round-trip a parametric project byte-for-byte when the embedded hash matches, fall back to a warned geometry parse when the file has been edited, reject a file that does not declare units, and warn explicitly that imported vectors are references rather than inferred walls (`src/studio/architect/exchange.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: verification is by the application’s own reader, not an independent one, and layer support is limited by the absence of CAD layers (C-06)."
+"I-02","Interoperability, imports and integrations","Native Windows DWG exchange","Binary file opens independently; unsupported objects are disclosed","partial","src/cad.rs","","ACAD; DWG; BCF; IDS","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). DWG import and export run through a bundled ACadSharp engine with magic-byte validation, a 16 MB cap, cancellation and round-trip verification, and an independent readback verified a 431-entity two-level fixture (`src-tauri/src/cad.rs`). Remaining: Windows desktop only, other platforms return an explicit unavailable result, and the installed-app path is unverified."
+"I-03","Interoperability, imports and integrations","IFC geometry and property exchange","Declared schema validates with correct object identity","partial","src/studio/architect/exchange.ts","","ACAD; DWG; BCF; IDS","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). DXF export writes a real ASCII drawing with header units, layer and linetype tables and LINE, LWPOLYLINE, CIRCLE, ARC and TEXT entities, and embeds the parametric project as SHA-256-bound chunks so an unmodified file round-trips to an identical project. A tampered file refuses to restore the stale embedded design and falls back to geometry, and a file that does not declare units is rejected (`src/studio/architect/exchange.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: no third-party CAD application has opened the exported file as proof."
+"I-04","Interoperability, imports and integrations","BCF issue exchange","Viewpoint, object references and discussion survive a second application","partial","src/studio/architect/ifc.ts","","ACAD; DWG; BCF; IDS","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). IFC4 export writes a spatial project, site and building hierarchy with deterministic identifiers and semantic void and fill relationships, asserted at three of each plus a material layer set usage (`src/studio/architect/ifc.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: IFC import does not exist, and no external IFC viewer or checker has validated the file."
